# run-cratonbench-gate.sh writes one directory per run here:
#
#   results/v<schema>/<utc>-<host>-<revision>/
#       manifest.tsv / manifest.json     environment + provenance
#       samples.tsv  / samples.json      EVERY raw sample, never only the summary
#       summary.tsv  / summary.json      p50/p90/p99/min/max/CV per phase
#       reliability-{pre,post}flight.*   the gate's verdict on the measurement
#
# Those are local measurement artifacts, not source, and a `git add -A` on this
# Windows checkout will happily sweep hundreds of them into a commit. They are
# ignored by default.
#
# To publish a run as evidence (an anchored baseline, a retraction, a half-gap
# writeup), add it deliberately:
#
#   git add -f regression-suite/perf/results/v1/<run-id>
#
# and reference the run_id from the evidence document, so the numbers in the
# document can be re-derived from the samples rather than believed.
v*/
